# Public `/pub/` Surface And robots.txt Sync

## Trigger conditions

- Any new user-facing React route or bookmark URL under the **`/pub/`** basename (see [`AppPub.jsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/AppPub.jsx)).
- Django/nginx/top-level URL changes that expose another crawlable HTML path under **`/pub/`**.
- Changes to [`nginx-static-files.conf`](services-conf/nginx-static-files.conf) SPA shell routing for **`/pub/`** or static **`/robots.txt`**.

## Required actions (same task)

1. Append the browser path (no hostname; include a trailing slash when it is the canonical directory URL) to **`PUBLIC_ROBOTS_ALLOW_PREFIXES`** in [`publicRobotsAllowPrefixes.js`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/config/publicRobotsAllowPrefixes.js) and run a frontend build so **`robots.txt`** is regenerated under **`hpcperfstats_site/static/frontend/`**.
2. Confirm the emitted body is **`User-agent: *`**, each **`Allow:`** line from that list (stable order), then **`Disallow: /`** (see [`robots-txt-format.js`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/robots-txt-format.js)).
3. Update assertions in [`test_web_pages_e2e.py`](hpcperfstats/site/machine/tests/test_web_pages_e2e.py) and [`test_web_pages_browser_e2e.py`](hpcperfstats/site/machine/tests/test_web_pages_browser_e2e.py) if needed: **`Allow:`** expectations are driven by the JS registry via [`public_robots_js_registry.py`](hpcperfstats/tests/public_robots_js_registry.py) helpers. WSGI must return **404** for **`/robots.txt`** and for **`/pub/`** HTML deep links (nginx-only shell), matching **`/machine/`** behavior.
4. Do **not** add **`Allow:`** entries for **`/api/pub/`** JSON unless product/security explicitly requires crawler access (default: APIs remain disallowed by the blanket **`Disallow: /`** except as overridden).

## Overlap

- [`web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc`](hpcperfstats/cursor-rules/web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc) — robots and SPA shell expectations for web E2E modules.
